This repository is a modified copy of OpenTalker/video-retalking at commit d32e8e5.
Files changed or added by nawta (2025-2026), as required by section 4(b) of the license.
Each modified source file also starts with a "Modified by nawta" comment.

Modified files
- README.md: added a section about this fork; updated install steps.
- requirements.txt: dlib 19.24.0 -> 19.24.6; numpy pinned to 2.2.6 instead of 1.23.4;
  added scikit-image 0.24.0, tqdm, and setuptools<81. An earlier commit in this fork also added
  pytorch-insightface, which nothing imports; it was removed again.
- inference.py, predict.py: import utils/torchvision_compat.py before basicsr.
- third_part/face3d/util/preprocess.py: removed the np.VisibleDeprecationWarning filter
  (the class no longer exists in NumPy 2).
- third_part/face3d/extract_kp_videos.py, utils/alignment_stit.py: use
  LandmarksType.TWO_D when face-alignment provides it (1.4 and later), else _2D.
- third_part/face_detection/utils.py, third_part/face3d/models/arcface_torch/eval_ijbc.py,
  third_part/face3d/models/arcface_torch/onnx_ijbc.py,
  third_part/face3d/models/arcface_torch/torch2onnx.py,
  third_part/face3d/models/arcface_torch/utils/plot.py: np.int -> int and
  np.float -> float (removed in NumPy 1.24).
- utils/inference_utils.py, third_part/face_detection/detection/sfd/sfd_detector.py,
  third_part/GPEN/face_parse/parse_model.py, third_part/GPEN/face_parse/face_parsing.py,
  third_part/GFPGAN/gfpgan/utils.py: torch.load with map_location='cpu', so checkpoints
  saved on a GPU load on machines without CUDA.

Added files
- NOTICE: this file.
- .python-version: the tested Python version (3.10).
- utils/torchvision_compat.py: maps torchvision.transforms.functional_tensor to
  torchvision.transforms.functional so that basicsr 1.4.2 imports on torchvision 0.17 and later.
- train.py: an unfinished training script skeleton. It is not part of upstream and does not run
  (see README.md).
